			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Fix circuit breaker trips from URI parsing and service isolation\n\nSubmodule sync bringing two critical fixes:\n\n1. **Mountain**: Fix false circuit breaker trips from URI parsing edge cases. Extensions frequently register file watchers on optional paths (e.g., `~/.roo/skills-*`, `.vscode/settings.json` in fresh workspaces) that don't exist. Mountain now catches benign \"path not found\" errors and records deferred entries instead of tripping the breaker. Additionally, Cocoon sends URIs in three formats (plain strings, objects with `external` field, legacy `scheme`+`path` objects), but only the `external` field was accepted. This caused `Diagnostic.Set` to trip the circuit breaker after 5 publishes, silencing all linters.\n\n2. **Output**: Fix ExposeWorkbenchAccessor transform silently failing. The import marker used single quotes but esbuild rewrites to double quotes post-bundle, causing the entire `__CEL_SERVICES__` patch to no-op and disabling all SkyBridge hooks. Also wraps each `invokeFunction` in its own try-IIFE so a single missing service doesn't throw the entire facade undefined.\n\nImpact: File watchers no longer fail on fresh workspaces. Language extension diagnostics now publish without triggering circuit breaker. All SkyBridge services (search, SCM, status bar, tree views) now initialize correctly.",
			"SHA": "0f4dbba95ab041db9b7cf1ec1c3c37151b1bfe74"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T01:41:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				102,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Accept numeric handles in FileWatcher and improve 404 detection\n\nSynchronize Mountain submodule with two bug fixes:\n\n1. **FileWatcher.rs**: Handle both numeric and string handle types in `RegisterWatcher` and `UnregisterWatcher`. The newer `NextProviderHandle()` returns a number while older callers pass strings. Previously, numeric handles were silently converted to empty strings causing failures.\n\n2. **MountainVinegRPCService.rs**: Extend 404-like error detection to include `FileSystem.ReadDirectory` and additional error message patterns (\"no such file or directory\", \"entity not found\", \"os error 2\"). Return distinct error code `-32004` for benign 404s so Cocoon's shim can classify them without regex string parsing, while `-32000` remains the catch-all for genuine failures.\n\nImpact: File watcher registration now works correctly regardless of handle type. Directory listing 404s are properly distinguished from genuine errors, improving error handling accuracy in Cocoon.",
			"SHA": "0d6755b26af812f8135b6a51610c3738e357e026"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T01:05:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				102,
				5
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Refactor env var handling with allow-list and fix errexit bug\n\nMulti-component synchronization and build system improvements:\n\n1. **TierEnvironment**: Switch from regex sweep (`^LAND_*`) to explicit allow-list of PascalCase keys (Pick, Require, Ship, Lodge, Extend, Probe, Skip, Mute, Wire, Install, Authorize, Beam, Report, Throttle, Buffer, Batch, Cap, Replay, Ask, Brand). This prevents unrelated OS/dev environment variables from polluting the diagnostic block. Also fix errexit bug by replacing `&&`-chain with `if [ -n ... ]; then ... fi` form - the `printenv` command exits non-zero for unset variables, which trips `set -e` when captured in command substitution.\n\n2. **turbo.json**: Remove `.env` files from globalDependencies since TierEnvironment.sh now handles env loading with explicit overlay sourcing.\n\n3. **Submodule sync**: Output adds RewritePerfBaselineWorker transform to fix timer service worker bootstrap crashes caused by Vite mangling `__name(...)` decoration in inlined Astro chunks.\n\n4. **Changelog**: Minor wording tweak (\"test suite\" → \"suite\").\n\nImpact: Build diagnostics now display only explicitly-allowlisted runtime variables, debug profiles no longer silently abort under errexit, and timer service worker boots correctly without reference errors.",
			"SHA": "a72870e9e95eaae2ec835dac7e09af244a6b727a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T23:07:16Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				103,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Element submodule with diagnostics pipeline and service worker fix\n\nMulti-component synchronization enabling language extension diagnostics to render in the editor UI:\n\n1. **Mountain**: Extend DiagnosticsChanged event with per-URI marker payloads and cap keyring crate logging to Warn level. The new `changedURIs` field enables direct `IMarkerService.changeOne()` calls without extra IPC round-trips.\n\n2. **Output**: Add RewriteNodeModulesPath transform to fix hardcoded `vs/../../node_modules` paths that were causing grammar/tokenization to silently fail (returning SPA fallback). Also expose IMarkerService on `__CEL_SERVICES__.Markers` for SkyBridge to push diagnostics.\n\n3. **Sky**: Add `sky://diagnostics/changed` handler that translates Mountain events into editor markers. Receives `{ owner, changedURIs: [{ uri, markers }] }` and calls `Markers.changeOne()` for each entry - enabling red squiggles and Problems panel population.\n\n4. **Worker**: Remove obsolete precache paths from Service Worker that caused `Failed to fetch` errors on every install (paths moved to Astro chunks).\n\nImpact: Language extension compile errors, lint warnings, and type errors from extensions like rust-analyzer, TypeScript, and ESLint now render as visible markers in the editor.",
			"SHA": "a630f00bcff2c393d74f5bb16eff01c8a9e73537"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T21:54:47Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				103,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Element submodule with Monaco worker fixes and polyfill telemetry\n\nSubmodule synchronization bringing stability improvements across multiple components:\n1. Mountain: Fix 404s for extension webview assets by extending vscode-file URI handling to support arbitrary authorities beyond \"vscode-app\". Also reduce extension-scanner logging noise by capping ignore-related targets to Warn level.\n2. Output: Fix Monaco worker bootstrap crashes with InjectWorkerBootstrapShim (injects __name/__defProp shim into webWorkerServiceImpl.js blob factory) and RewriteNestedWorkerBootstrap (replaces .toString() pattern with JSON.stringified source). Switch RewriteStaticBlockSelfRef from hardcoded whitelist to auto-detection. Add __LAND_POLYFILL_TELEMETRY__ hook.\n3. Sky: Wire polyfill telemetry through PostHog bridge to capture errors via PH.captureException with categorized properties.\n4. Wind: Remove deprecated Electron polyfill shims as functionality moves to Mountain's native Rust implementations.\n\nImpact: Extension webview assets now load correctly, Monaco language workers no longer crash on startup, production polyfill failures are captured for debugging, and obsolete Electron shims are cleaned up.",
			"SHA": "cf08b5fec5bd1eead24636eadf43c81f8f5b9584"
		}
	],
